    },
    {
      "id": "th-1019-3",
      "at": "2026-10-19T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "You don't need weights to hit harder.\n\nTurn the back foot. Relax until impact. Exhale sharp on every shot.\n\nPower starts on the floor. No pivot, no punch.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "power-without-weights",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T21:36:06Z",
      "thread_id": "18111799088183306",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DesPM4LgV6K"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1020-1",
      "at": "2026-10-20T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "The hardest punch isn't the strongest one.\n\nIt's the one they walk into.\n\nTiming beats strength every time.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "power-without-weights",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-20T11:36:02Z",
      "thread_id": "18115162027838143",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DetvU1_oOqc"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1020-2",
      "at": "2026-10-20T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Training alone this week?\n\nWhat's your go-to solo session?\n\nShadowboxing, bag rounds, footwork, or tape study?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "dangerous-without-a-partner",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-20T16:32:14Z",
      "thread_id": "18107458187523064",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DeuRN-_kc_q"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1020-3",
      "at": "2026-10-20T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "No partner? Give every bag round a rule.\n\nOnly counters this round. Only body shots the next.\n\nYou build reactions, not just punches.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "dangerous-without-a-partner",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-20T21:36:07Z",
      "thread_id": "18411428233094157",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Deu0ACBAZ4l"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1021-1",
      "at": "2026-10-21T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Fear before a fight isn't the problem.\n\nFeel it. Name it. Walk out anyway.\n\nThat's the entire skill.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "go-anyway",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-21T11:36:01Z",
      "thread_id": "17940524586385988",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DewUHv9FLr_"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1021-2",
      "at": "2026-10-21T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Started combat sports late?\n\nHow old were you when you walked into your first gym?\n\nCurious how many of you are out there.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "started-late",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-21T16:32:59Z",
      "thread_id": "18100925747630241",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Dew2GqOlTdO"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1021-3",
      "at": "2026-10-21T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "When training suddenly feels harder, most people think they're getting worse.\n\nUsually it's the opposite.\n\nYou're starting to notice mistakes you couldn't see before. That's what leveling up feels like from the inside.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "about-to-level-up",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-21T21:36:01Z",
      "thread_id": "18132443602748373",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/DexYyMikqip"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1022-1",
      "at": "2026-10-22T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Stop caring how it looks.\n\nStart caring if it works.\n\nThat switch is when you actually start getting good.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "about-to-level-up",
      "status": "posted",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-22T11:35:59Z",
      "thread_id": "18095202590244313",
      "url": "https://www.threads.com/@matteofights/post/Dey46bsFUEY"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1022-2",
      "at": "2026-10-22T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Which one is you?\n\n1. Training feels harder, not easier\n2. The guys who used to beat you are struggling now\n3. Sparring feels slower than it used to\n\nDrop the number.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "about-to-level-up",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1022-3",
      "at": "2026-10-22T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Started late? Ask more questions than anyone in the gym.\n\nOne question a session to the best person there.\n\nMost will help. Nobody's ever annoyed by someone who wants to learn.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "started-late",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-15T18:18:31Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1023-1",
      "at": "2026-10-23T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Hard sparring every week makes most beginners worse, not tougher.\n\nYou learn to survive, not to fight. Light rounds with one rule teach more than a war you just get through.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1023-2",
      "at": "2026-10-23T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Cardio, hands or head: which one goes first for you in round three?\n\nPick one. Then say what you do when it goes.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1023-3",
      "at": "2026-10-23T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "I had a ruptured appendix the day before a fight.\n\nThat's the closest I've come to quitting. What kept me in it wasn't a plan. It was \"I can't give up.\"\n\nNot smart advice. Just the honest answer.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1024-1",
      "at": "2026-10-24T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Shadowboxing without a target is cardio with your hands up.\n\nPick an opponent. Give him a lefty stance and a habit of dropping his right. Then fight him for three rounds.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1024-2",
      "at": "2026-10-24T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "What did your first coach get wrong?\n\nOr what did they get right that you only understood a year later?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1024-3",
      "at": "2026-10-24T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Slept five hours? Do technique rounds today, not hard ones.\n\nTired sparring teaches bad habits and gets people hurt. Save the war for a day you can actually think.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1025-1",
      "at": "2026-10-25T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "Comparing yourself to the guy a year ahead is how people quit.\n\nHe's already made a year of mistakes you haven't. Compare yourself to you in March.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1025-2",
      "at": "2026-10-25T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "What do you still do from month one, even though you know it's wrong?\n\nCommon one: dropping the back hand after the jab.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1025-3",
      "at": "2026-10-25T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "chain",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Your jab feels weak? Check these five things before you blame your arm.",
      "chain": [
        "1. Elbow.\nIf it flares out, the punch loses its straight line. Keep it pointing at the floor until the arm extends.",
        "2. Shoulder.\nRotate it up toward your chin at the end. Free reach, and it covers your jaw.",
        "3. Return.\nA jab that stays out is a push. Fire it and bring it back at the same speed.",
        "4. Feet.\nIf you step and then punch, the jab lands half a beat late. Move together.",
        "5. Breath.\nExhale on contact. Holding your breath makes the arm stiff."
      ],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1026-1",
      "at": "2026-10-26T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "I tore a knee ligament in a street fight.\n\nI took a guy down like a BJJ guy, on pavement. The mat has rules. Pavement doesn't. Training for a sport and training for the street are two different jobs.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1026-2",
      "at": "2026-10-26T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Hard sparring or ten rounds on the pads: which leaves you more sore?\n\nAnd which one made you better?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1026-3",
      "at": "2026-10-26T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "tip",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Three minutes of arm circles isn't a warm up.\n\nSkip rope until you sweat, then shadowbox at half speed for two rounds. Your first hard breath shouldn't come in your first real round.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1027-1",
      "at": "2026-10-27T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Try the new move in sparring. Even if you lose the round.\n\nWinning with your best three tricks teaches you nothing. Failing with a new one shows you what to fix.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1027-2",
      "at": "2026-10-27T16:30:00Z",
      "kind": "question",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Music in the gym or no music?\n\nSome people can't think with it. Some can't start without it. Which one are you?",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1027-3",
      "at": "2026-10-27T21:30:00Z",
      "kind": "story",
      "topic": "Fight Psychology",
      "text": "My first Muay Thai fight was a draw.\n\nI hit him with a right hand while the ref was separating us. He went down. It was not clean at all.\n\nOfficial result: a draw. The scorecard doesn't care what you remember.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "founder",
      "status": "queued",
      "approved": true,
      "approved_note": "Matteo: approved via dashboard (2026-10-18T15:34:38Z)"
    },
    {
      "id": "th-1028-1",
      "at": "2026-10-28T11:30:00Z",
      "kind": "take",
      "topic": "Combat Sports",
      "text": "Rest isn't lazy.\n\nSkipping it is how you end up with a six week injury. Sleep, eat real food, take the day off. The boring half of training is the half that holds the rest together.",
      "chain": [],
      "from": "craft",
